adjectives.txt and nouns.txt were written from scratch for this package (Claude Sonnet 5.5,
2026-10-28). No existing word list was copied, so there is no third-party source or license to
record. Words were picked by hand and then filtered:

- lowercase ASCII letters, 3 to 9 letters, sorted, no duplicates, nothing in both lists
- dropped on purpose: first names (rose, ivy, hazel), brands and product names (jaguar, mustang,
  swift), words that are offensive, violent, sexual, medical, political or religious in some
  common reading, and words that are insulting in some common reading (sloth, weasel, baboon)
- nouns lean concrete and easy to spell: animals, plants, objects, places in nature

An Opus review of the lists on 2026-10-28 removed what the first pass missed: names and brands
(teddy, martin, marten, rowan, rosemary, thermos), nouns in the adjective list (laser, quantum,
micro, noon, morning, evening, artisan), non-words and odd fits (proto, sunkissed, just,
fledgling, butte), words with an unkind reading (shady, sly, twisted, shallow, nutty, benign,
shaggy, raccoon), hard spellings (corydoras, currawong, kinkajou), and beech, a soundalike of
beach.
